#pragma code_page(65001)
// res/lang/or.rc -- Odia, the strings of the interface for `[general] language = "or"`.
//
// Stage E108, group A: the two string tables of this language -- the dialog block and the menu
// block -- in the order of en.rc. The rules every table obeys stand in app.rc above the #include
// lines; where each string is seen and how much room it has is res/lang/context.tsv;
// tests/l10n.rs holds this file to en.rc. The glossary of the language is l10n\glossary\or.tsv
// of the control contour.
//
// ⚠ In an .rc string a backslash is an escape -- one backslash is written as two -- and a double
// quote inside a string is written as two double quotes. The code page line above is this
// file's own: without it rc.exe reads the file in the ANSI code page, silently.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Odia — `[general] language = "or"`.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
